  "goals": [
    {
      "text": "Name the five stages of a page load",
      "step": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "See why every handshake costs a full round trip",
      "step": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "Find where the time actually goes",
      "step": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut round trips with HTTP/3 and connection reuse",
      "step": 7
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "short": "One click",
      "chapter": "setup",
      "title": "What happens when you press Enter?",
      "body": [
        "Ines, in Lisbon, types <code>plotline.app</code> — a garden-planning site — and presses Enter. Half a second later her garden appears. It feels like one action, but it is a <b>relay of five jobs</b>, each waiting for the one before it.",
        "The plotline server sits in a data centre in Virginia, about 6,000 km away. Keep that distance in mind: it will matter far more than how fast the server is."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "A <span class=\"term\">round trip</span> (RTT) is one message there and the reply back. Lisbon ⇄ Virginia costs about <b>90 ms</b>, however small the message."
      },
      "metrics": {
        "dns": null,
        "connect": null,
        "request": null,
        "download": null,
        "total": null
      },
