    {
      "short": "TCP",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Shake hands across the ocean",
      "body": [
        "Next the laptop opens a <span class=\"term\">TCP connection</span> to that address. TCP promises the bytes arrive complete and in order, but first both sides agree to talk: <code>SYN</code>, <code>SYN-ACK</code>, <code>ACK</code>.",
        "The client may send data right behind its final ACK, so the handshake costs exactly <b>one round trip — 90 ms</b>. Nothing useful has been exchanged yet."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "A faster connection doesn't help here. The handshake is tiny; what it pays for is <b>distance</b>."
      },
      "changes": [
        "~ DNS answer cached, resolvers idle",
        "+ TCP handshake laptop ⇄ server",
        "~ Connect 0 → 90 ms"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "dns": 30,
        "connect": 90,
        "request": null,
        "download": null,
        "total": 120
      },
