    {
      "short": "TLS",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Agree on a secret",
      "body": [
        "The address is <code>https://</code>, so before any page is requested the two sides run a <span class=\"term\">TLS handshake</span>: the server proves who it is with a certificate, and both derive shared encryption keys.",
        "With TLS 1.3 this costs <b>one more round trip</b> (TLS 1.2 needed two). Connect time is now 180 ms — and Ines still hasn't asked for her garden."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "warn",
        "text": "Two of the jobs so far are pure ceremony, and <b>every new connection</b> to a far-away server pays for them again."
      },
      "changes": [
        "~ Wire now carries the TLS hello and certificate",
        "+ Timeline card",
        "~ Connect 90 → 180 ms"
      ],
