    {
      "short": "Request",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Finally, the question",
      "body": [
        "Over the encrypted connection the browser sends <code>GET /garden</code>. Half a round trip to get there, half to come back: <b>90 ms</b> of travel.",
        "In between, the server does the real work — checks the session, asks Postgres for Ines's planting beds, renders HTML. That <span class=\"term\">server time</span> is about <b>60 ms</b>, so the request phase totals 150 ms."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Those 60 ms are the only part the backend team directly controls. Hold on to that number."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Postgres behind the web server",
        "~ Request + server 0 → 150 ms"
      ],
