    {
      "short": "Download",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Bytes don't arrive all at once",
      "body": [
        "The reply is 64 KB of HTML. A brand-new connection doesn't know how much the path can carry, so the server starts cautiously — about 14 KB — then waits for acknowledgements before sending more. This ramp-up is <span class=\"term\">slow start</span>.",
        "The sending window roughly doubles each round trip (14 KB, then 28 KB, then the rest), so 64 KB needs about <b>two more round trips — 180 ms</b>. Bigger pages need more."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "On a fresh long-distance connection, size costs <b>round trips</b>, not just bandwidth. Trimming 30 KB can save a whole RTT."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ 64 KB response streaming back",
        "~ Download 0 → 180 ms"
      ],
