      "short": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "title": "One click, five jobs",
      "body": [
        "<ul class=\"takeaways\"><li>A page load is a relay: <b>DNS → TCP → TLS → request → download</b>, each waiting on the last.</li><li>Every handshake costs a full round trip, and distance sets the price of a round trip.</li><li>Server work is often a small slice of what the user waits for.</li><li>Go faster with <b>fewer trips</b> (connection reuse, HTTP/3, caching) or <b>shorter trips</b> (servers closer to users).</li></ul>"
      ],
